  "worked_solution": "Notice that our inequality\n\n$$\n(x+1)(x-4)\\le 0,\n$$\n\nis a \"*less than or equal to*\" inequality. Therefore, we need to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola \n\n$$\ny=(x+1)(x-4)\n$$\n\nis *below* the $x$-axis or *touches* this axis. We mark these values of $x$ in blue in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972108/assets/291593bb5f8e2dda1ba506bc1d00e004afe60199e731521e5d6abd321669d8f4.png)\n\nSo, the solution to the inequality is $-1\\le x\\le 4.$",
